div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1080443-subtle-displays-of-wealth?p=1080736#post1080736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, hotels could potentially be secured against sunlight more easily than motels.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think either would leave a vampire pretty defenseless come morning. Big windows are kind of a thing. The few hotels I've stayed at with an 'indoor' side had a big skylight in the interior area, which meant every room in the place got a strong dose of sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:50:18-07:00","id":1081471,"title":"","content":"if the vamps wanting to disguise feeding as a sexual encounter? id agree, he needs to be back home well before dawn","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:49:24-07:00","id":1081514,"title":"","content":"Well, Kindred with high Humanity can have sex and feed at the same time, which should be a particularly addictive and potent combination in my opinion. I doubt that anyone would be able to be satisfied with a 'normal' orgasm after experiencing a 'feeding enhanced' orgasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:57:57-07:00","id":1081545,"title":"","content":"yes, but was wondering, a reason to check out a hotel, rather then motel room, when he doesnt iintend to stay there all night?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T13:19:40-07:00","id":1081558,"title":"","content":"Motels would be honestly preferable. They have less security and, as long as someone checks out in the morning, no one cares as long as there are no bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:54:09-07:00","id":1081632,"title":"","content":"same thing I was thinking, just seeing if their was something I was missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T00:55:41-07:00","id":1081743,"title":"","content":"Some other subtle signs of wealth might be: well-tailored clothing with no tags or labels; functional ornamentation (specifically, the cuff buttons on men's suit coats being functional rather than just sewn over a closed cuff); on the flip-side, almost borderline disfunctionality - if she looks like she was poured into that skin-tight dress that she can barely move in, and you can't see any zippers, odds are it cost a shitload of money. <br /> <br /> Also, men might carry a money-clip, or a favorite pen or cigar, and women may have a tiny clutch purse (and almost everyone has their phone), but the majority of stuff that you and I carry around I our pockets, well... Wealthy people have someone else carry all that stuff for them (wallets ruin the line of the suit, you see). Cheque books, car keys, business cards - that's all handled by someone else. <br /> <br /> You can also have wealthy people constantly rearranging items - a passive-aggressive psychological tic of marking dominance. <br /> <br /> On a more humorous note, people that were born to wealth often have no idea about the cost of necessities. It's not uncommon for them to overestimate the price of basics, like paying $50 for milk (and one unnamed person made the gaff of claiming migrant workers were paid $20 an hour to pick fruit), or being surprised when they receive change (giving money <i>back</i> to someone confuses them). <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:40:22-07:00","id":1081787,"title":"","content":"Another sign off true wealth among elite men are cuff-links. The value of cuff-links worn on a suit tends to be a good correlation to the wealth of the individual unless they are clueless. Wealthy women tend to wear clothing that fits like a second skin, any teenage girl can find clothing so tight that they can barely walk, it just takes a few hours at the mall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:27:03-07:00","id":1081875,"title":"","content":"If we are talking about Garou, don't forget high end cologne or bath products. A person who uses a 99 cent bottle of suave is going to smell different than a person who buys high end products from the salon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T18:33:53-07:00","id":1082468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1080443-subtle-displays-of-wealth?p=1081743#post1081743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, men might carry a money-clip, or a favorite pen or cigar, and women may have a tiny clutch purse (and almost everyone has their phone), but the majority of stuff that you and I carry around I our pockets, well... Wealthy people have someone else carry all that stuff for them (wallets ruin the line of the suit, you see). Cheque books, car keys, business cards - that's all handled by someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, one huge sign of wealth is just having a lackey at their side at all times. They carry their stuff, open doors, drive the car (assuming the car doesn't come with its own separate driver), answer the calls (the boss can't be bothered unless it's important), and generally arrange all the things their employer is simply too rich to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:13:42-07:00","id":1082574,"title":"","content":"noticed something<br /> <br /> On a lot of movies, in the old days,even the middle class would often have a servant or two, these days only the richest do, and they have far smaller staffs then they used to.<br /> <br /> I've heard its partialy because of automation.<br /> <br /> allowing 1 person to do work once done by several<br /> <br /> partialy because of mininum wage laws, anything else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:59:30-07:00","id":1082586,"title":"","content":"Less of a sense of obligation to the lower classes as well (as the wealthy would rather gamble their money in the stock market than provide someone with work). In the USA, the cost (wages, benefits, taxes, etc) associated with maintaining a good servant is around $120,000 per year ($60,000 per year for wages and bonuses, $40,000 per year for benefits and pension, $20,000 per year for taxes and equiment). Now, you can pay less, but you get what you pay for, and you generally want good servants.<br /> <br /> So, it depends on how much of your discretionary income you are willing to spend on servants. In the USA, one servant per $1,000,000 (or fraction thereof) would be the most that you would see, but most billionaires do not have large staffs. In the developing world though, servants are security, and anyone without sufficient servants would soon regret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 04-23-2017, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:21:21-07:00","id":1082622,"title":"","content":"Another reason for a Garou wealthy enough to hire Servants to only Consider Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Oh, a way to justify a Rich Silver Fang finding Kin he could hire as a maid?<br /> <br /> (Im putting in a application as a busboy at a restaraunt to clean tables, hey its work) <br /> <br /> Oh a Vampire that lives in a Condo Hotel? <br /> <br /> thoughts on getting ghouls a suite of their own, as opposed to just sleeping in your living room?<br /> <br /> as I see it.<br /> <br /> Getting them their own suite, prevents awkward questions.<br /> <br /> Downside, is their not there on as short a notice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:21:19-07:00","id":1082716,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a variety of ways to run each scenario. Silver Fangs could offer Kin a job as bodyguards masquerading as maids, giving them both salaries, and explain that maids are perfectly positioned as bodyguards because no one notices them and that they can only trust their Kin to serve them. Kindred could just blood band the entire staff, and ghoul only the people who would have access to their suite, in order to gain adequate security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T12:55:33-07:00","id":1082742,"title":"","content":"If tthe hotel isnt too high profile, like the Plaza in New york.<br /> <br /> <br /> which is only Hotel I know of selling Condos.<br /> <br /> though Im sure theirs much cheaper condo's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:40:08-07:00","id":1083083,"title":"","content":"Another aspect: Rich people's time is more valuable to them than money. <br /> <br /> A rich Glasswalker may buy a condo for a short term mission rather than have to search for a hotel each time they visit the mission location. To a Bone Gnawer, this is an extravagant waste of money, but to the rich Glasswalker the convenience our weighs the monetary cost. <br /> <br /> After the mission, the Glasswalker may even sell the place and make a profit. Maybe rub it in her pack mate's face by donating the profits to the Bone Gnawer's favorite charity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T18:36:53-07:00","id":1083254,"title":"","content":"Well, they place a higher monetary value on time. If someone make $100 million per year (Resources 5), an hour of their time is worth at least $50,000. They will not work an extra hour a year unless they will make much more than $50,000 and may actually be willing to spend $1 million to save an hour a week. At that level of wealth, they hire a gourmet cook because the cook will save them the 21 hours a week that they would waste going to 5-star restaurants. They will hire people to select the outfits that they wear everyday because they do not want to waste ten minutes every morning deciding what to wear that day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T19:16:10-07:00","id":1083267,"title":"","content":"Oh curious? If your rich enough to be able to afford a mansion,but the wife wants to cook for her husband occasionaly.would it be reasonable to have a separate Kitchen? (so you dont have to give the staff the day off)<br /> <br /> Oh if your only resources 3 or 4, relatively affluent but not super Rich. How strong would the Incentive to just go to the Restaraunt on Site of your Gated Community or hotel, rather then leave to go out into town be?<br /> <br /> went to outback for Filet Mignon first time in years recently.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-25-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:14:10-07:00","id":1083429,"title":"","content":"Well, the majority of couples just give the servants an evening off in that case. Private kitchens are not unknown as well within the living quarters if people value their privacy during the evenings. Resources 3 may live in a gated community, but most gated communities do not possess restaurants (some will just have a private restaurant in the clubhouse, but they are just there for convenience rather than quality). Resources 4 means that you are likely too wealthy to live in a gated community, though you may own a few houses in gated communities in localities that you often visit (or condos).<br /> <br /> People eat in hotel restaurants because they want company. If you just want convenience, you just order room service or have a delivery service go to a restaurant of your choice. Wealth gives you options and wealthy characters have lots of options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T07:12:51-07:00","id":1083445,"title":"","content":"I looked at prices of room service, 2 or 3 places... couldnt imagine getting it, rather then going to hotel restaraunt.<br /> <br /> since the decors VERY fancy<br /> <br /> Almost went to the restaraunt the last Grand Masquerade was at... but thought it was a bit much at $32 Just for the meal itself<br /> <br /> I spend that much for a meal sometimes, because I get a drink or 2 with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\